# Primary & secondary buttons

Every **primary** and **secondary** button in the app must use one shared style.
Prefer `HLButton` or the exported class constants — do not invent per-screen
button chrome.

**Scope:** apply across the whole product UI in one pass whenever button chrome
changes — dashboards, modals, drawers, empty states — not one button at a time
when a teammate spots a mismatch. Frozen `src/shell/*` files stay untouched.

## Fixed size — never change

| Spec | Value | Tailwind |
|------|-------|----------|
| **Total height** | **36px** | `h-9` + `box-border` |
| Padding top/bottom | 8px | `py-2` |
| Padding left/right | 14px | `px-3.5` |
| Border radius | 8px | `rounded-lg` |
| Gap (icon + label) | 8px | `gap-2` |
| Shadow | `0 1px 2px 0 rgba(16, 24, 40, 0.05)` | `shadow-xs` |
| Label | 14px semibold | `text-[14px] font-semibold leading-none` |

`box-border` + `h-9` keeps the **1px border inside** the 36px box. If you omit
`h-9` and only use `py-2`, content + padding + borders measure **~39px** — that
is a bug.

```
display: inline-flex
box-sizing: border-box
height: 36px
padding: 8px 14px
justify-content: center
align-items: center
gap: 8px
border-radius: 8px
```

## Primary

```
border: 1px solid #155EEF (primary-600)
background: #155EEF (primary-600)
color: white
hover: primary-700 bg + border
```

```jsx
import HLButton, { BTN_PRIMARY } from '../HLButton.jsx'

// Preferred
<HLButton variant="primary" color="blue" size="sm">Re-scan site</HLButton>

// Raw <button> when HLButton cannot be used
<button type="button" className={BTN_PRIMARY}>Re-scan site</button>
```

## Secondary

```
border: 1px solid #D0D5DD (gray-300)
background: #FFF
color: gray-700
hover: bg-gray-50
```

```jsx
import HLButton, { BTN_SECONDARY } from '../HLButton.jsx'

<HLButton variant="secondary" color="gray" size="sm">Compare scans</HLButton>

<button type="button" className={BTN_SECONDARY}>Compare scans</button>
```

## Exported constants (source of truth)

```
src/components/HLButton.jsx → BTN_BASE, BTN_PRIMARY, BTN_SECONDARY
```

`modalBtnPrimary` / `modalBtnSecondary` in `HLModal.jsx` alias these same
strings — do not fork modal button sizing.

When this spec changes, update `BTN_BASE` first; every `BTN_*` consumer and
`HLButton` size `sm` (36px) must stay aligned.

## Do not

- Do not ship a primary/secondary CTA at **39px** (or any height other than 36px).
- Do not use `h-8` (32px) on primary/secondary CTAs.
- Do not replace `py-2 px-3.5` with `py-1.5` / `px-3` / `px-4` / `h-9 px-4` alone.
- Do not use `border-gray-200` on secondary — use `border-gray-300`.
- Do not use purple (`bg-purple-600`) for standard primary CTAs — primary is
  blue (`primary-600` / `#155EEF`). Purple remains for AI-specific accents only
  when the product explicitly calls for it.
- Do not drop `shadow-xs` on these two variants.
- Do not hand-roll primary/secondary classes — always `BTN_PRIMARY` /
  `BTN_SECONDARY` or `HLButton`.
- Icon-only square controls (settings gear, close) are **not** primary/secondary
  CTAs — they keep their own sizing.

## Before finishing button work

- [ ] Primary/secondary use `HLButton` or `BTN_PRIMARY` / `BTN_SECONDARY`.
- [ ] Computed height is **36px** (inspect if unsure).
- [ ] Padding is **8px 14px** (`py-2 px-3.5`), radius `8px`, `shadow-xs` present.
- [ ] Primary border+bg are `primary-600`; secondary border is `gray-300`.
- [ ] No leftover bespoke `h-8` / `py-1.5` / `border-gray-200` / missing shadow.
